\fs14\
\f1 \b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 NSColorWell is an NSControl for selecting and displaying a single color value. An example of an NSColorWell object (or simply\i  color well\i0 ) is found in NSColorPanel, which uses a color well to display the current color selection. A color well is available from the Palettes panel of Interface Builder.\
\fs14\
\fs28 An application can have one or more active color wells. You can activate multiple color wells by invoking the \b activate:\b0  method with NO as its argument. When a mouse-down event occurs on a color well\'27s border, it becomes the only active color well. When a color well becomes active, it brings up the color panel also.\
\fs14\
\fs28 The \b mouseDown:\b0  method enables a color well to send its color to another color well or any other subclass of NSView that implements the NSDraggingDestination protocol.\
\fs14\
